#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example demonstrates an external steer controller implemented in MATLAB. It is described in the Tech Memo available from the Help menu > Technical Memos > Example: Extending a Model with VS Commands and the API
#
#If you are using a 64-bit version of MATLAB, you MUST switch the linked Model dataset to the 64-bit version. You must also have a compatible C compiler installed on your machine.
#
#If you want to use the feature which allows you to save multiple sets of results, the ring control must be set prior generating the files for the run.
#
#To make the run:
#1. click the button "Generate Files for this Run",
#2. from within MATLAB, run the file "Steer_control.m" from the folder Extensions\Custom_M.
#
#For comparison, this simulation is overlaid with another example, "Steer Controller with VS Commands." That example has the same vehicle but uses a steer controller implemented with VS Commands.
